From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Abdalla Ashry <abdallah.ashry@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: add Bluetooth for NanoPi R28S

The Bluetooth part of the AIC8800D80 module is connected to UART2.
Describe it like the FriendlyElec vendor device tree so the hci_uart
AIC protocol driver binds to it.

Signed-off-by: Abdalla Ashry <abdallah.ashry@hotmail.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-r28s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-r28s.dts
@@ -137,6 +137,11 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart2m1_xfer>, <&uart2m1_ctsn>, <&uart2m1_rtsn>;
 	uart-has-rtscts;
 	status = "okay";
+
+	bluetooth {
+		compatible = "cvte,aic8800-bt";
+		device-wake-gpios = <&gpio1 RK_PB4 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+	};
 };
 
 &usb_host0_xhci {
